\f1\fs22 \'93Johnny thinks it\'92s his meeting,\'94 Hayley said to the mirror.\
\'93I saw,\'94 Sarah answered.\
Johnny was sitting at the head of the table like he had dogs at his feet and a fire in the hearth. Dr Quark sat Johnny\'92s immediate right. As Sarah came in, he\'92d had his head down and wouldn\'92t look at her. Perhaps he feared a beheading. They both deserved a beheading, right there in the conference room, the blood spilling hot on the carpet in front of the cool of the rainforest peering in through the floor-to-ceiling windows.\
Sarah blinked that image away and waited for Little Clinton to give her the shift she needed.\
\'93I\'92m heading out,\'94 Hayley called.\
\'93Okay,\'94 Sarah replied. \'93Don\'92t execute anyone. At least not until I\'92ve had a cup of tea.\'94\
Hayley was still standing when Sarah reemerged.\
\'93Good,\'94 Johnny said. \'93Now we can begin.\'94\
Sarah selected a teabag, dropped it in a cup and poured hot water over. She took her time jiggling the bag and stirring four spoons of sugar into it. She decided against milk\'97it had been turning her stomach of late. With saucer in hand, Sarah turned and observed where the men had declared their territories around the table. Chip had arrived and left a couple of seats between him and Johnny on the near side. He was staring blankly out at the rainforest, probably counting the threats in it.\
Sarah took to the nearest seat\'97in the middle of the long side, a few places down from Chip. Hayley sat at her side.\
Johnny started to call the meeting to order but Sarah swiftly raised a hand at him. Whatever he intended to blather about died in his throat in the middle of a syllable.\
\'93I hear the washing machine has grown some arms,\'94 Sarah said tersely. \'93Three arms, to be exact.\'94\
Johnny slid a document pack down the table to Sarah. \'93If you refer to the\'97\'94\
\'93Who is in charge of this project?\'94 Sarah demanded.\
The ice in the bar fridge chilled a little more.\
Johnny started, \'93Technically and operationally\'97\'94\
