\cf2 \'93Tax the adverbs, Stoat,\'94 Sarah thundered, and felt a little woozy for it. \'93Who. Is. In. Charge.\'94\
\'93You are, young Sarah,\'94 Kleo said quietly.\
Sarah rolled her eyes. Being referred to as young was not helping.\
Kleo\'92s eyes sparkled and Sarah suspected he knew a thing or two about her. \'93Do you know what health condition I was born with?\'94 she asked him.\
Kleo held his answer back while he considered his options. \'93Limb girdle\'97\'94\
\'93Thank you,\'94 Sarah quietly snapped then turned to Johnny. \'93I explicitly directed that we acquire no more kebabs. Yet the washing machine seems to have attracted three more monkeys.\'94\
Tree ferns crowded the glass outside, as if they were leaning in to hear the answer. Coachwood trunks stood over  layers of green close enough to make the room feel buried in the bush rather than overlooking it.\
\'93Have you acquired more kebabs?\'94 Sarah asked Johnny, interrogation style.\
\'93He has,\'94 Chip answered tersely.\
Sarah was momentarily distracted by bright movement outside. Wings flapping, getting closer. A king parrot landed outside the window and appeared to look in. It tapped on the glass. He appeared proud, and amused. His scarlet-red head was as bright as a traffic light against the cool greens in the dappled light. His neck and breast were a deeper red in shadow. He turned and modelled his green wings and tail, then tapped the glass again.\
Sarah wondered if the bird was checking out the Sages; certainly their robes today weren\'92t too unlike parrot colours and markings. Apparently, Sarah was in a conference with parrots.\
\'93From where have you acquired more kebabs?\'94\
Johnny sat back, relaxed, as if he thought he\'92d repossessed the upper hand in the exchange. \'93From the Elvi.\'94 Johnny enjoyed saying that.\
Sarah chilled. \'93What?\'94\
\'93Indeed,\'94 Johnny lauded, while aching for Sarah to just like hum for a change. \'93We met at the local crematorium.\'94\
\'93What? They were just selling them off the back of a truck?\'94 Hayley injected.\
\'93Out of a van, actually.\'94\
Chip appeared like he was trying to stop himself from combusting. Dr Quark was still not meeting anyone\'92s gaze.\
Johnny was enjoying this. \'93The answer to who has cornered the market in kebabs is: the Elvi, your loyal and doting subjects.\'94\
Chip looked sideways at Sarah.\
\'93Cornered the market?\'94 Sarah parroted and was drawn to the bird outside the window that appeared to be laughing at her, then to the Sages, who weren\'92t laughing but still looked like parrots anyway. \'93DO they have more?\'94\
A cold thought occurred to her; she wondered if Chanta had anything to do with this.\
\'93They have guitar cases full of them.\'94 Johnny tried to cover his fear of that.\
\'93Oddly specific,\'94 Hayley whispered in Sarah\'92s ear.\
Sarah nodded. It didn\'92t ring as the kind of lie Johnny would construct. She exhaled and let her head nod as she thought. \
\'93The new High Elvis seems to have a different agenda to the previous one,\'94 Johnny added.\
\'93Hardly surprising,\'94 Sarah said. \'93The government of the day recently tried to exterminate them.\'94 Are the Elvi planning some kind of reprisal? Sarah had confidence that they would tell her if they were.\
\'93I would strenuously advise against warring with the Elvi,\'94 the Solo parrot counselled.\
\'93That\'92s not on the table,\'94 Sarah reacted.\
Chip growled and scratched his eyebrow.\
\'93If I may, Ms Jacobson,\'94 the Solo parrot led.\
\'93Proceed,\'94 Sarah said.\
The Solo parrot gestured to the Chilo parrot. The parrot at the window flew away.\
\'93You will recall that Mr Stoat has been calling for a pentagram configuration since late September,\'94 Chilo said.\
\'93I have made certain Fridge Force documents available to Ms Jacobson,\'94 Chip countered as if impatient with a dim maths student. \'93The probability of disastrous side-effects escalates exponentially with each kebab that\'92s introduced into a coherent field.\'94\
Dr Quark looked up for this first time. \'93I would like to review the evidence.\'94\
\'93You don\'92t need to, and you can\'92t,\'94 Chip said.\
\'93In the interests of science\'97\'94\
\'93In the interests of public\'97of 
\f2\i planetary
\f1\i0  safety\'97\'94\
\'93Please,\'94 Kleo cut in. \'93May we present our findings?\'94\
\'93Your findings?\'94 Chip was incredulous. \'93You couldn\'92t find a stick of gum in your pocket.\'94\
Solo was offended. He reached under his robe and produced a stick of gum. So did the other two Sages. They seemed like they might hold their talismans up until Shrove Tuesday, so Sarah asked Chilo to go ahead.\
\'93Here\'92s comes the prophecy,\'94 Chip mocked.\
\'93Here comes the telemetry,\'94 Chilo countered, and gestured over his device. Screens on three sides of the room 
\f3\fs24 \cf0 \outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 each took turned
\f1\fs22 \cf2 \outl0\strokewidth0 lit with a schematic of. Two traces began moving around it.\
Sarah recognised the motion of two monkeys swinging on their bar. They ran, slowed, and accelerated like each took turns chasing the other.\
\'93You will observe the motion of the primary arms seeming to pause at various points and oscillate over a fixed point for some time,\'94 Chilo said.\
\'93We have generated heat maps from the positioning data to show where the primary arms stuttered. \'93Chilo ran an animation of the motion heat map. Two regions of red appeared and disappeared, over and over, at varying points in the rail.\
Sarah recognised the shimmying frequency she\'92d seen during the test.\
\'93Now, I\'92ll show you a heat map of positioning rolled up from the whole test,\'94 Chilo said.\
The image was on the screen for a few seconds before Johnny began to slow-clap. \'93Well done, Chilo!\'94\
Sarah clenched her jaw with almost as much force as Chip did. What the screens showed, as stark as fire were very pronounced, small concentrated regions of red around the ellipse.\
There were five of them.\
For a flourish, Chilo had prepared a final slide of the ellipse, with lines drawn connecting the centres of the red regions to form a star.\
\'93A pentagram!\'94 Johnny was jubilant.\
\'93I want to see the data and the modelling,\'94 Dr Quark said.\
Chip looked at Quark. \'93So do I.\'94\
Chilo agreed and gestured over his device. Beeps and rings sounded out about the room. Though Johnny had no idea, his tablet played three notes that mimicked the first bar of the chorus from a song that, in some tidier universes, was called \'93You\'92re so Vain.\'94\
\'93You\'92d better explain this.\'94 Chip was surly.\
\'93The instability of the washing machine is due to this stuttering,\'94 Chilo said.\
\'93We already know that,\'94 Chip said. \'93That\'92s why the washing machine is a failure.\'94\
\'93Only because it\'92s programmed to react to instability in the kebabs,\'94 Chilo said.\
\'93And this proves it cannot stabilise them,\'94 Chip hurried back with.\
\'93It proves it cannot stabilise 
\f2\i two
\f1\i0  kebabs,\'94 Solo countered.\
Chip slammed the table. \'93You\'92re twisting a failure into an excuse to escalate the failure.\'94\
\'93The washing machine wants five kebabs, young Mr Stockwell,\'94 Kleo said. Sarah thought he sounded sad.\
\'93The problem is, the machine is trying to maintain five harmonic relationships with only two kebabs,\'94 Chilo said. Sarah thought he was enjoying this rather too much.\
\'93I was right!\'94 Johnny slapped the table; it sounded foppish compared to Chip\'92s bear-sized slam.\
Chilo took a breath. \'93May I proceed, Ms Jacobson?\'94\
Sarah gave him a nod.\
Chilo touched his device. Three more primary arms appeared on the schematics on the screens around the room.\
\'93I\'92ll run a simulation that follows the changes in nominal kebab rotation speed to match the test.\'94\
The five arms moved.\
\'93I\'92ve sped up the simulation. It only takes a minute.\'94\
The five arms moved in a more elaborate game of run and chase. It was quickly obvious that monkeys were swinging more smoothly. The stuttering was completely absent and lap times were faster. Then the arms slowed down and settled into individual regions around the ellipse. While they started to oscillate within their own regions, they were smooth and slow. The swinging above and below the elliptical plane was gentle and graceful. A new pentagram appeared overlaid on the simulation. Its geometry stretched and rotated, but it appeared controlled and deliberate, as easy as breathing.\
\'93Note there is no catastrophic vibration in the apparatus,\'94 Chilo said.\
Chip shook his head. \'93That just means it\'92s more dangerous than it\'92s ever been.\'94\
\'93You\'92re talking as though solving an engineering problem is somehow bad news. I\'92d say we\'92ve risen to a new point of equilibrium,\'94 Johnny said, a little too smugly.\
\'93I want to see the analysis and run the simulations,\'94 Dr Quark stated.\
\'93By all means, verify the results,\'94 Johnny said.\
\'93Verify. Or repudiate,\'94 Dr Quark said.\
\'93Very good,\'94 Chilo said in the tone most retained for when they said \'93fine\'94 and meant anything but.\
Sarah watched the five monkeys behaving themselves, then looked out the windows. The rainforest seemed as cool and refreshing as ever.\
Sarah searched for parrots.
